item('applicability','The fixed obligation is the literal AppendFuture.Response precondition in S-pipeline-contract: Error must return before Response access. Actual pipelineDecode is a caller of that interface. The fixed test passes actual InmemTransport futures through forwarding wrappers; it does not invent a future contract or feed a synthetic malformed response. In-memory and network producers call respond before publishing, which establishes readiness and explains why this access may work in practice. That protection does not constitute the documented Error method invocation/return, and the interface contains no Consumer-specific exemption. The property is therefore applicable as local implementation semantics, not as a proof of invalid log support.',['No conclusion about custom transport failure behavior or invalid commitment.'])
item('decomposition','The selected necessary condition is Error-return-before-Response-invocation for one future. The monitor does not require that Error success be equivalent to Response success, demand any particular RPC outcome, or infer eventual progress from an absent event. It also does not establish that respecting this ordering is sufficient for safe quorum support. S-pipeline checks response term and Success, S-append-future simply returns the pointer, and S-inmem-pipeline publishes after respond; these are protective/alternative mechanisms for data readiness, not compliance with the literal access precondition. A healthy permitted execution prefix and successful response can coexist with the observed ordering violation.',['Only method order is checked; transport-error handling, request correlation under faults and consensus effects remain independent.'])
item('checker_correspondence','Inspected fixed plan.json and assurance_generated_test.go for artifact 6ac27453c3ba4c08ac32729d6b783b1b and raw execution 59614562669b48149511f09b7690de2d. NewRaft, bootstrap, AddVoter and Apply run actual workers. The wrapper maps each concrete AppendFuture pointer to a unique observational wrapper for both AppendEntries return and Consumer delivery; the producer retains its own original future and completes it with respond, not Error. Consumer forwarding preserves order. The observed Error method delegates and records return; Response records that per-object flag before delegating the real getter. pipelineDecode performs these accesses in its decoder goroutine, so the atomic flag is not an invented response property. A single CAS selects the first actual Response independently of the flag, avoiding selection by failing outcome. The event response_invoked admits this operation; response_returned records actual underlying getter completion and the saved entry-time flag. Stable history/operation identifiers correlate exactly one pair. Raw events show term 2, previous index 4, zero entries, error_returned_before_call=false, followed by a real successful term-2 response and driver_complete after Apply. Empty entries do not exempt the future method contract. The oracle compares only the false flag with required true; it does not label successful response data as bad or claim a match index was advanced. The source has no Error call in pipelineDecode; wrappers do not suppress one. Shutdown runs independently and the execution completed without timeout. Underlying completion before the wrapper itself returns is sufficient here because the prohibited access occurred at invocation and the delegated getter returned.',['Only the first observed Response call is in the bounded monitor.','The run does not reproduce a failure of the underlying RPC or an application consequence.'],['S-bootstrap','S-config-append','S-startup','S-replicate-loop','S-inmem-init'])
